tly smaller than \\(|\\mathcal Q_k|\\).  Hence an even \\(k>0\\) is impossible.  \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.  Covering an odd\u2011sized triangle by sunny lines\n\nLet \\(m\\ge 1\\) be **odd** and write \\(m=2t+1\\).  Define the family\n\n\\[\nL_j:\\; y = x + j ,\\qquad j=-t,-t+1,\\dots ,t .\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nAll these lines have slope \\(1\\); therefore each of them is sunny, and they are clearly distinct.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### Lemma 2  \nThe \\(m\\) lines \\(\\{L_j\\}_{j=-t}^{t}\\) together contain every point of \\(\\mathcal P_m\\).\n\n*Proof.*  \nFix \\(j\\).  A point \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal P_m\\) lies on \\(L_j\\) iff \\(b=a+j\\).  \nThe conditions \\(1\\le a\\le m\\), \\(1\\le b\\le m\\) and \\(a+b\\le m+1\\) become\n\n\\[\n1\\le a\\le m,\\qquad 1\\le a+j\\le m,\\qquad 2a+j\\le m+1 .\n\\]\n\nThe first two inequalities give \\(1\\le a\\le m-|j|\\); the third one is automatically satisfied for such \\(a\\).  Hence the points of \\(\\mathcal P_m\\) on \\(L_j\\) are exactly\n\\[\n\\{(a,a+j)\\mid a=1,2,\\dots ,m-|j|\\}.\n\\]\nThus \\(L_j\\) contributes the whole \u201c\\(j\\)-th diagonal\u2019\u2019 of the triangle.  As \\(j\\) runs through \\(-t,\\dots ,t\\) these diagonals partition \\(\\mathcal P_m\\); consequently every point of \\(\\mathcal P_m\\) lies on one of the lines \\(L_j\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Full construction for every admissible \\(k\\)\n\nLet \\(k\\) satisfy the condition of Lemma\u202f1, i.e. \\(k=0\\) or \\(k\\) is odd and \\(1\\le k\\le n\\).\n\n*Step 1 \u2013 non\u2011sunny part.*  \nTake the horizontal lines  \n\n\\[\nH_i:\\; y=i\\qquad (i=1,2,\\dots ,n-k).\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\n\nThese \\(n-k\\) lines are distinct, non\u2011sunny, and they cover all points of \\(\\mathcal P_n\\) whose second coordinate does not exceed \\(n-k\\).\n\n*Step 2 \u2013 the remaining 